Let's look at the volume of cement transported with a single truck. A single truck transports $x$ liters of cement every trip, and it does $y$ trips. So in total, it transports $xy$ liters:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\left(x\,\dfrac{\text{liters}}{\text{trip}}\right)\left(y\,\text{trips}\right)
\\\\
&=xy\,\dfrac{\text{liters}}{\cancel{\text{trip}}}\cdot\,\cancel{\text{trips}}
\\\\
&=xy\,\text{liters}
\end{align}$
